\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The terminal feedback contract. At decision tick $t$, the selector sees $S_t$ and $A_t$ and chooses one provider before any current output is observed. The terminal record is split into output and runtime status; the frozen endpoint judge then yields chemical correctness only after termination. Runtime failure and chemical correctness form the selected terminal outcome, which waits in a selected-only queue until $\tau _t=t+1+D$. The relay update is visible to the first action at or after release; for $D=0$, this is the next action.}}{5}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:lifecycle}{{2}{5}{The terminal feedback contract. At decision tick $t$, the selector sees $S_t$ and $A_t$ and chooses one provider before any current output is observed. The terminal record is split into output and runtime status; the frozen endpoint judge then yields chemical correctness only after termination. Runtime failure and chemical correctness form the selected terminal outcome, which waits in a selected-only queue until $\tau _t=t+1+D$. The relay update is visible to the first action at or after release; for $D=0$, this is the next action}{figure.caption.6}{}}
